---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Write for Us — GlobalsBlog | Guest Post Guidelines"
	description="Contribute to GlobalsBlog. Write guest posts on travel, auto, or beauty for an Indian audience. Get a do-follow backlink, author profile, and social promotion."
>
	<section class="content-page">
		<div class="content-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">Write for GlobalsBlog</p>
			<h1>Share your knowledge with India's travel, auto &amp; beauty readers.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Are you passionate about travel, cars, EVs, or skincare? Do you enjoy
				researching a topic and explaining it clearly? GlobalsBlog welcomes contributors to write
				for us and become part of our growing author network. Whether you're a travel blogger, an
				auto enthusiast, a beauty content creator, or simply someone with useful, well-researched
				knowledge to share — if you've got something valuable to say, we'd love to feature your voice.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="content-grid">
			<article class="content-card">
				<h2>Who can write for GlobalsBlog?</h2>
				<p>
					If you're knowledgeable about travel, automobiles, or beauty — and can
					explain things clearly for Indian readers — you're welcome to pitch us. We accept
					contributions from travel bloggers, auto journalists, beauty content creators,
					mechanics, skincare enthusiasts, and general writers with strong research skills.
					You don't need to be a professional writer. You need to know your subject and be able
					to write in a way that genuinely helps the reader.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">Why write for GlobalsBlog?</h2>
				<p>
					GlobalsBlog is an independent editorial platform covering Travel, Auto, and Beauty
					for Indian readers — built around practical, research-backed content and free
					interactive calculators. Our audience ranges from travellers planning their next trip
					and car buyers comparing options, to readers looking for skincare advice suited to
					Indian skin and climate.
				</p>
				<p>
					When you write for GlobalsBlog, your article goes on a platform that values depth,
					real numbers, and genuinely useful advice — not filler content. We're building a
					knowledge resource for Indian readers, one well-researched article at a time.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">What you get as a contributor</h2>
				<ul class="content-list">
					<li>Exposure to a growing audience of Indian readers across three categories</li>
					<li>An author bio with a do-follow backlink to your site or portfolio</li>
					<li>Your article shared across our social media channels</li>
					<li>A byline and author profile page on GlobalsBlog</li>
					<li>Fast review and publishing turnaround (2–3 business days after approval)</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">Topics we accept</h2>
				<p>We're open to well-researched, India-relevant content across our three categories:</p>
				<ul class="content-list">
					<li><strong>Travel</strong> — Destination guides, itineraries, budget travel tips, road trips, adventure activities, train and flight travel</li>
					<li><strong>Auto</strong> — Car reviews, EV guides, comparisons, buying guides, maintenance tips, RTO processes, fuel efficiency</li>
					<li><strong>Beauty</strong> — Skincare routines, makeup guides, ingredient explainers, product comparisons for Indian skin and climate</li>
				</ul>
				<p>If your idea genuinely helps an Indian reader make a decision or understand something better, we're interested.</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">Guest post guidelines</h2>
				<ul class="detail-list">
					<li><strong>Word count:</strong> Minimum 1,000–1,500 words — in-depth, informative content is preferred</li>
					<li><strong>Originality:</strong> 100% original, unpublished content. No plagiarism and no AI-generated-only submissions — write from research or real experience</li>
					<li><strong>Tone:</strong> Conversational, clear, and easy to follow — written for a real reader, not a search engine</li>
					<li><strong>Formatting:</strong> Use H2/H3 headings, short paragraphs, and bullet points where useful</li>
					<li><strong>Links:</strong> One do-follow link to your site or portfolio is allowed — no spammy, unrelated, or excessive linking</li>
					<li><strong>Images:</strong> Royalty-free images (Pexels, Unsplash, Freepik) or your own, with credit where required</li>
					<li><strong>No promotions:</strong> Articles should inform the reader, not advertise a brand, product, or service directly</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">What we don't accept</h2>
				<p>
					To maintain the quality of GlobalsBlog, we do not accept content that is plagiarized,
					overly promotional, or generated entirely by AI without genuine human research and
					editing. We avoid publishing articles that lack depth, offer no real value to readers,
					or repeat topics already covered on the site.
				</p>
				<p>
					Submissions must be relevant to one of our three categories — Travel, Auto, or
					Beauty — with a clear focus on Indian readers. Content that falls outside our niche or
					appears to be written purely for link-building will be rejected.
				</p>
			</article>

			<aside>
				<div class="content-card content-card-accent" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">
					<h2>How to pitch</h2>
					<ol class="detail-list" style="padding-left:1.1rem;list-style:decimal">
						<li>
							Email your pitch or full draft to
							<span class="email-reveal" data-e="contact" data-d="globalsblog.com">contact [at] globalsblog.com</span>
							with the subject line "Guest Post — [Your Topic]"
						</li>
						<li>Include a short author bio (40–50 words) and a link to your website, portfolio, or LinkedIn</li>
						<li>Mention which category your article fits — Travel, Auto, or Beauty</li>
						<li>Our editorial team will review and respond within 2–5 business days</li>
						<li>Once accepted, we'll edit, format, and publish — then send you the live link</li>
					</ol>
				</div>

				<div class="content-card" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">
					<h2>Quick checklist</h2>
					<ul class="content-list">
						<li>Original, unpublished, and well-researched</li>
						<li>1,000–1,500 words, written for Indian readers</li>
						<li>Clear H2/H3 structure with short paragraphs</li>
						<li>One relevant do-follow link, no spam</li>
						<li>Royalty-free or credited images</li>
						<li>Informative — not a product advertisement</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="content-card">
					<h2>Have questions first?</h2>
					<p>
						Not sure if your idea fits? Send us a one-line pitch before writing the full article
						and we'll let you know.
					</p>
					<p style="margin-top:0.75rem">
						<a href="/contact-us">Visit the contact page →</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</aside>
		</div>

		<div class="content-card" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
			<h2>Browse our categories</h2>
			<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem;margin-top:0.5rem">
				<a href="/category/travel" style="padding:0.45rem 1rem;border-radius:100px;background:rgba(182,91,46,0.08);color:var(--accent);font-size:0.88rem;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;">Travel</a>
				<a href="/category/auto" style="padding:0.45rem 1rem;border-radius:100px;background:rgba(182,91,46,0.08);color:var(--accent);font-size:0.88rem;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;">Auto</a>
				<a href="/category/beauty" style="padding:0.45rem 1rem;border-radius:100px;background:rgba(182,91,46,0.08);color:var(--accent);font-size:0.88rem;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;">Beauty</a>
				<a href="/about" style="padding:0.45rem 1rem;border-radius:100px;background:rgba(182,91,46,0.08);color:var(--accent);font-size:0.88rem;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;">About GlobalsBlog</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll('.email-reveal').forEach(function (el) {
    var email = el.dataset.e + '@' + el.dataset.d;
    var a = document.createElement('a');
    a.href = 'mailto:' + email;
    a.textContent = email;
    el.parentNode.replaceChild(a, el);
  });
</script>
